\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The loop at a glance, in the shape ruled 260819. A PREPARE loop ({\fontfamily  {pzd}\fontencoding  {U}\fontseries  {m}\fontshape  {n}\selectfont  \char 172} OUTLINE, {\fontfamily  {pzd}\fontencoding  {U}\fontseries  {m}\fontshape  {n}\selectfont  \char 173} PROBE, {\fontfamily  {pzd}\fontencoding  {U}\fontseries  {m}\fontshape  {n}\selectfont  \char 174} EVIDENCE) repeats until the plan is self-consistent, because evidence does not confirm a plan; it changes it. ONE gate leads out: four machine checks (coverage, address, value, shape), then a person's \texttt  {approved:}. Everything after the gate runs unattended ({\fontfamily  {pzd}\fontencoding  {U}\fontseries  {m}\fontshape  {n}\selectfont  \char 175} DRAFT, {\fontfamily  {pzd}\fontencoding  {U}\fontseries  {m}\fontshape  {n}\selectfont  \char 176} REVISE with {\fontfamily  {pzd}\fontencoding  {U}\fontseries  {m}\fontshape  {n}\selectfont  \char 177} COMPILE folded in) until {\fontfamily  {pzd}\fontencoding  {U}\fontseries  {m}\fontshape  {n}\selectfont  \char 178} CHECK, which a person judges and which reaches CLOSE or returns the page to any earlier phase. Red ticks are the five stops reserved for a person; no machine may write one.}}{1}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:qpw00-loop-at-a-glance}{{1}{1}{}{figure.1}{}}
\gdef \@abspage@last{1}
